WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.860
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.970
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:17.540
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:26.310
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:34.050
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.520
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.390
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:44.130
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:48.790
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.470
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.470 --> 00:01:01.140
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.520
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:12.160
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.060
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:22.300
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:32.410
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:37.150
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:41.880
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.990
<i>Kosuke Asazuki...</i>

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:54.290
<i>He knew things only my
brother would know...</i>

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:56.860
<i>What are the Blade Children?</i>

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.830
<i>Why are they after me?</i>

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.160
<i>What exactly was my brother pursuing?</i>

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.070
Have you been paying attention?

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:07.170
Nope, not one bit.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.700
Come to the faculty office later.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.140
Now then, let's continue.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:17.650
"The Misty Gallows"

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.640
"Faculty Office"

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:23.180
"Faculty Office"
Your grades and behavior
aren't exactly "bad".

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:26.580
Your lack of cooperation is also within
the bounds of your individuality.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.390
Normally, I wouldn't call you
in here for something like this.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.720
Then what did I do wrong?

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.260
You're too good at giving up.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.500
Don't you think that with
just a little more effort

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:41.970
you would have the ability to rise
to a level normal people never could?

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.240
Of course not.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.440
I'm just a boring old high school student.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.940
You shouldn't give up on
your potential at your age.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:55.780
The power within you may be
needed by someone someday.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:58.720
Is that all you want to tell me?

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.910
A nightmarish destiny
will soon draw near you.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.640
He's better than I thought,
that Little Narumi.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.580
He guessed the card right,
and he saw through Stage #2.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.050
His name's Narumi for a reason, huh?

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:31.280
Your checkmate was weak.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.950
It wasn't an un-winnable game.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:36.010
Well excuse me...

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.430
But does Little Narumi
really have the ability

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:46.030
to change the fate of the Blade Children?

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.470
That depends on how the plan goes.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.670
Yeah, the so-called "plan"...

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:54.170
They call it fate because people
can't change it, you know...

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:57.910
But our fate was made by people...

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.670
Doesn't that make it all
the more unchangeable?

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.820
Will you stop lying?!

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.690
I...I didn't break it!

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:13.760
<i>What's going on, Suzuki-sensei?</i>

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.560
<i>Imazato-sensei...</i>

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:17.290
This student broke this window,

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:20.260
but she lies about it and
refuses to apologize!

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.830
I'm not lying!

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:25.370
A rock really did fly from
outside and break the glass!

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:28.870
Then why would there be
glass fragments outside too?!

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.710
If a rock came flying from outside,

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:33.040
the fragments would have
landed on the inside!

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:36.510
But, I didn't...

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.050
Enough of your excuses!

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:40.380
<i>Now, now, Suzuki-sensei...</i>

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.420
<i>Please stay out of this, Imazato-sensei!</i>

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.990
Hold on.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:48.390
Don't you know that glass has elasticity?

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.130
Glass bends when it's hit,

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:53.830
and its elasticity tries
to return it to normal.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.500
The same is true when it breaks.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.670
Because of the elasticity,
the broken glass fragments

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:59.760
fly off in both directions.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:04.580
It's known as the "Blowback Effect".

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.370
This girl isn't lying.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:08.680
Now that you know,

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:12.010
clean up the glass and apologize to her.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:16.580
<i>So he really is his younger brother...</i>

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:23.630
I've heard rumors that you're
making moves on your own.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.630
And?

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.030
Your way of doing things

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:29.500
seems like an attempt to kill Ayumu Narumi.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:32.200
There'd be no point otherwise.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:36.710
At his current level, he IS
lacking something definitive.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:39.580
He doesn't believe in his own ability.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:43.880
But there's no doubt that an
irreplaceable power lies within him.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:47.590
Do you intend to crush your
last hope with your own hands?

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:50.490
If he really is the key
to changing our fate,

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.920
then he will not be crushed
beneath our strength.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.460
Rutherford...

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:55.890
If you're not going to stop,

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:58.620
then I'm going to switch
sides and hunt you instead.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.400
The wind has taken an ill turn...

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.670
Did this much happen when it was good?

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:10.670
Imazato will be a nuisance as an enemy.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:13.740
He knows too much about us.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:17.480
It would be dangerous if information
found its way to Little Narumi.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.280
You seem to have a lot to say,
so I'll leave him to you.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:23.250
He's not the kind of guy
who's easily taken care of.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.960
Plus I'd be recognized.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:28.860
In that case, have Rio assist you.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.860
Rio is reliable...

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.130
But I can't handle being around her...

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.240
Stop right there!

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.700
What do you want?

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.710
I have some terrific news!

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.510
That's great. Bye.

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:48.770
<i>I got some information on Asazuki-san!</i>

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:51.600
Asazuki?

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.250
Kosuke Asazuki.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:57.020
According to his date of birth,
he's currently 17 years old.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.720
Oh, and he's a Virgo.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:02.090
He attended Moriwaka Middle
School until he was 14,

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:07.900
but in his 2nd year there he
disappeared after injuring a teacher.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:08.800
Any family?

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.730
There's no information on his father

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:15.040
and his mother died in an
accident when he was three.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:17.170
That's a pretty good
intelligence network you have.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:19.040
This was nothing!

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.910
Just you watch.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:26.850
In a week's time I'll even
tell you where he lives.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:29.150
<i>Talk about scary...</i>

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:32.690
<i>But Kosuke Asazuki...</i>

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:37.800
<i>From his background he
must move pretty nimbly.</i>

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:41.890
<i>It would seem he has a bit
of organized support too.</i>

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:48.510
Um...

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.900
<i>Narumi-san...</i>

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.310
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.250
Aren't you forgetting something?

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.120
<i>"Thank you, Hiyono-chan!</i>

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:01.490
Thanks to you the truth has been played!"

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:04.760
Moving words of gratitude like that!

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:07.920
Huh? Why would I say that?

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:13.000
Hiyono Punch!

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.000
Huh?

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.000
Um...

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.170
Um...

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:20.200
What?

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:23.000
Thank you for this afternoon!

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.120
She's not too bright...

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.020
Nope...

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:35.420
What did you do for her?

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:38.960
Nothing worth being thanked for...

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.860
<i>That's not true, Narumi-kun.</i>

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:44.800
What do you want?

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:48.730
It wasn't much, but you
did help that girl earlier.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.970
That's an invaluable skill.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:54.470
It's important to have faith in yourself
even when someone refutes you...

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.910
<i>You're definitely right
about that, Imazato-sensei!</i>

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:05.420
I want to talk to you
about the Blade Children.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:07.080
Do you feel like listening?

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:11.420
I'm putting myself at risk
contacting you like this.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:14.560
Act like nothing is out of the ordinary.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:16.930
What do you know?

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:21.000
There are all kinds of people moving
around, more than you can imagine.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.800
All with their various intentions.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:25.940
Alright, I'll listen.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.740
Who are you and what is
being expected of me?

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:33.510
Six o'clock in the student
guidance room. Alright?

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.500
Yeah.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.850
<i>Imazato-sensei.</i>

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:58.240
Still 5:00...

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:02.870
<i>I just can't seem to find
Asazuki-san's current address...</i>

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:05.580
He doesn't seem to have
a permanent residence...

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.310
Hey, something happened
in the school building!

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:08.980
What?

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:12.320
Let's go check it out!

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.380
What do you think's going on?

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.280
Let's find out.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:22.130
What happened?

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:25.220
<i>Imazato-sensei collapsed!</i>

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.630
We need an ambulance!

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:39.610
Well?

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.600
We're too late. He's dead.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:47.820
I want to talk to you
about the Blade Children.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:49.680
Do you feel like listening?

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:54.350
<i>Damn it...Who the hell did this?!</i>

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.600
Hey, you can't just barge in and...

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.550
Both his breathing and pulse have stopped.

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:18.720
Rigor mortis is starting to set in!

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:21.020
An ambulance won't help now.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:23.520
Call the police! Hurry!

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:24.990
Right!

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:27.520
Who first found him?

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:28.990
Me...

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:31.330
When, and how?

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:32.360
Just now.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:35.130
The door was open and
I saw him on the floor

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.130
when I passed by it.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:39.940
How do you suppose he died?

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:43.300
It doesn't look like he's
been injured at all...

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:48.110
He died of gas poisoning.

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:49.950
But...

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.250
...I don't smell any gas.

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:56.020
The doors and windows are open
so it's long since dissipated.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:59.610
And besides, it wasn't
city gas or propane.

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:11.940
Say, it's pretty cold in here...

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:14.240
I wonder if the air conditioner is on...

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:16.610
That's the murder weapon.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:17.980
Murder weapon?

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:20.710
You're saying someone's
responsible for this?

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.150
The timing is too good -

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:26.380
he died a strange death immediately
after trying to tell me a secret.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:29.320
The Blade Children are
probably the ones responsible.

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:31.150
What on earth is going on?!

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:34.620
<i>Stay out. Imazato-sensei has been murdered.</i>

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.250
Close the school gate immediately
and wait for the police.

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.760
This was a homicide.

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:43.870
The murder took place just past 4:00 pm.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:46.200
The killer was a student
at Tsukiomi Academy

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.740
who was in this area at the time.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:51.610
They're very likely still on campus.

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:54.680
They're between 150 and
155 centimeters tall,

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.410
and their shoe size
is 22 centimeters.

00:12:57.410 --> 00:12:59.180
The killer is female.

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:00.980
How can you tell that?

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:05.020
The melody of logic
always plays the truth.

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:07.760
With your abilities, how many
suspects can you narrow it down to

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.360
with what little data we have?

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:12.430
Give me three days and I'll
have it under 20 people!

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:13.130
I'm counting on you.

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:14.630
I'm being counted on!

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:15.730
<i>Just you watch.</i>

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.600
<i>I'll force you out, Blade Children!</i>

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:23.070
"Science Lab"

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:29.450
I knew it...

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.450
There's nothing here...

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.520
The killer took it.

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:34.790
The murder weapon, that is.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:36.290
Murder weapon?

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:37.690
Dry ice.

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:51.070
Alright!

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:54.940
Here's a listing of the heights
of all the students at school!

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:56.370
I'll use this list as a base

00:13:56.370 --> 00:14:00.810
and extract all the girls with heights
between 150 and 155 centimeters.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:09.090
Hmm, that still leaves us
with over 50 people...

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:11.760
This is where my talents
really start to shine!

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:12.820
What are you gonna do?

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:16.690
Carefully inspect the things
these people did today,

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:18.100
create a movement map,

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:19.930
and determine the number of people they met

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:22.660
and how much time they spent in transit!

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:26.240
By tomorrow evening I
should have information

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:28.270
about every one of them!

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:32.080
Your information-gathering
abilities are really something...

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:35.110
Aren't they, though?

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:39.450
By the way, what does dry ice
have to do with gas poisoning?

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:42.790
Dry ice is frozen carbon dioxide.

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:46.420
Imazato died of carbon dioxide poisoning.

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:47.920
Carbon dioxide?

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.060
Yeah.

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:53.530
It's in the air we breathe so
many people think it's safe,

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:57.200
but in concentrated amounts it'll
poison your system and kill you,

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:58.770
just like carbon monoxide.

00:14:58.770 --> 00:14:59.940
Yikes...

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:03.810
<i>So Imazato-sensei died when he
entered the classroom full of dry ice</i>

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:06.540
that had evaporated into carbon dioxide gas?

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:07.640
Yep.

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:10.680
The temperature of dry ice is
below -70 degrees Celsius.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:12.680
I don't know how much was used,

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.490
but when it all evaporated the
temperature in the classroom

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:17.250
must have fallen pretty low...

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.960
Around the teacher's desk were marks

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:24.360
where water vapor in the air condensed.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:28.170
So then the dry ice was placed
beneath the desk, right?

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:29.300
Yeah.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.770
And when it had all vaporized,

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:33.740
the killer called Imazato into the room

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:38.240
and detained him by talking
to him until it was too late.

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:39.980
I see...

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:42.310
Since the killer was in
the same room as him,

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:44.110
he didn't notice right away.

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:46.980
Plus carbon dioxide is
tasteless and odorless.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:51.720
But then why didn't the killer
suffer from gas poisoning too?

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.760
Carbon dioxide is heavier
than oxygen and nitrogen

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:56.730
so it would collect at the bottom.

00:15:56.730 --> 00:16:00.230
The killer was sitting in a seat
at the very top of the classroom

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:02.030
so they didn't breathe the gas.

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:05.940
So that's why you checked
the seats at the top...

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.510
The killer turned the audio-visual room

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:11.370
into an invisible gallows of mist
specifically meant for Imazato

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.240
and then escaped.

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:15.510
So what about the killer's
height and shoe size?

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:18.450
There were fresh footprints left behind.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:19.750
They probably stepped in a wet spot

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:22.020
since the temperature fell so quickly.

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:25.790
I determined their height from the
distance between those footprints.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.560
And their gender?

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:31.190
Judging from the height and shoe
size, it was unlikely a boy.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:32.800
One last question.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:35.370
Why do you think it was
one of the students?

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:40.370
The body showed no signs of
resistance or attempts to escape.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:42.310
Probably by the time he realized it,

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:45.180
he had already breathed in
large amounts of carbon dioxide.

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:48.310
In which case, it's a high possibility
that the killer was a student

00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:50.980
since it wouldn't be unnatural
for them to be there.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:55.010
It was probably someone who
looked very unlikely to ever kill...

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:59.260
You have some nerve to
suddenly call for me

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:01.350
and then make me carry that heavy stuff...

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.530
You know that dry ice is
heavier than regular ice, right?

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:07.260
That's why I called for you.

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:09.530
<i>Thanks for your help, Kosuke-kun!</i>

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:13.260
But I'll admit, it was impressive
for such a quick scheme.

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:18.410
Who's there?!

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:19.480
<i>Imazato-sensei.</i>

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:22.350
I'd like to discuss something with you.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:24.040
Takeuchi?

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:32.090
What's wrong? Are you cold?

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:34.560
Yeah...

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:36.830
Is the air conditioning on, I wonder?

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:38.430
It might be cold...

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:43.300
...because an enemy is nearby.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:44.570
What?!

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:48.100
Do you intend to oppose us,
no matter what?

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.070
You're...

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:52.140
One of the Blade Children...Rio Takeuchi.

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:54.740
Even a girl like you, too?!

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:59.580
<i>Could you refrain from telling
Ayumu Narumi-san about us?</i>

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:02.050
Don't you think that's a little unfair?

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:05.460
Do you actually believe fate is fair?

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:06.390
If it is,

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:09.990
then I wonder if the Blade Children
would have been born at all...

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:13.000
I never knew you were so
pessimistic about life...

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.000
I'm not pessimistic.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.830
I'm simply looking at
reality in a calm manner.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:21.940
Now could you answer my question?

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:25.510
<i>I can't let Narumi-kun die here...</i>

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:30.150
I've decided to switch sides
and hunt you instead...

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:32.150
If you're insistent on getting in our way,

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:33.680
then there's no other choice.

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:37.980
You're...going to kill me?

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.010
<i>Imazato-sensei.</i>

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.680
Goodbye.

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:18.830
That little brother of his is really good.

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:21.200
You think?

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:24.500
I mean look, he instantly depicted
a correct image of the culprit

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:26.100
and then laid out a net.

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:27.400
Talk about amazing!

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:31.170
So you mean he has impressive
powers of perception and deduction?

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:33.380
That's not all.

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:35.350
He has a type of extrasensory power.

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:36.680
But it's only natural, huh?

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:40.350
You basically challenged Little Narumi
by killing him on school grounds.

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:41.850
What did you expect?

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:45.360
<i>But Imazato-sensei was just
about to leak information to him...</i>

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:49.160
We never expected him
to attack so quickly...

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.160
Don't worry about it.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:54.100
That girl's information
abilities are amazing,

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:57.130
but only enough to narrow it
down to about 10 suspects.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:59.740
After that it's a stalemate
with nowhere to move.

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:02.140
They'll never catch us.

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:06.140
<i>You're so stupid, Kosuke-kun!</i>

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:09.510
His little brother isn't the
type to give up so easily!

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:13.480
If this keeps up, we're going
to be forced out into the open...

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:16.940
Though we'll probably be
the ones to win in the end...

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:25.260
Your deductions are really good,

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:28.330
but we just don't have enough base data...

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:32.270
I don't think I can get it under 10 people.

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:34.340
Could you go any further from that?

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:35.540
Are you kidding me?

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:38.410
My deductions are fundamentally
too weak as it is.

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:40.110
Even if we do narrow it down to one person

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:42.350
it's all over if they play dumb.

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:46.050
Then isn't doing this pointless?

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:49.790
No, there's one more clue we need.

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:53.120
The snare net is already laid out...

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:55.830
I will be the one who wins in the end.

00:20:55.830 --> 00:21:04.160
<i>Little did we suspect that things were
about to take such a drastic turn...</i>

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:11.410
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:18.110
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:36.270
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:41.900
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:47.810
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.810 --> 00:21:54.380
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.380 --> 00:22:00.120
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:05.330
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.330 --> 00:22:11.170
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.170 --> 00:22:22.780
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:28.550
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.550 --> 00:22:34.850
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:38.950 --> 00:22:43.120
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:43.120 --> 00:22:44.960
A really interesting menu
item has been discovered

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:46.460
in a coffee shop by the station!

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:50.160
It's name? Natto Pumpkin Squid
Ink Strawberry Parfait Deluxe!

00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:52.930
I need to get info on it right away!

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:58.030
Next episode's highlight is when a
lost cat visits the newspaper office!

00:22:58.030 --> 00:23:00.240
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:01.840
Blind Spot in the Snare Net

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:04.610
Don't miss the serious turn
of events in the next episode!

00:23:04.610 --> 00:23:06.870
That's all for today's Hiyono's Playhouse!
